Bridge: remote mode across machines

- bridge.py: token-authed read-only HTTP service that runs ON the Hermes
  host and serves the exact data layer (state, schedule, content, content
  read) plus host metrics from that machine — fails closed without a key
- portal remote mode: DataProvider sources state/schedule/content/read from
  the bridge; host metrics now report the Hermes box, not the portal VM

Proven cross-machine: bridge on the server (192.168.100.177), portal on the
WSL box in remote mode pointing at it. The WSL portal renders the SERVER
fleet — 8 agents, 405 runs, 4 platforms, 21 content docs, 1 cron job — and
the SERVER host metrics, all over the LAN with bearer auth. Chat/runs still
need the target host :8642 gateway enabled (honest gateway-down state).

